			"Message": "chore(Monorepo): Synchronize elements with transport registry and source compilation pipeline\n\nThis commit advances all major submodules, introducing critical architectural improvements to the transport layer and build pipeline.\n\n## Transport Layer Architecture\n\n### Common: Transport Registry for Dynamic Selection\n- Implemented `TransportRegistry` for managing multiple transport strategies (IPC, gRPC, WASM) at runtime\n- Added `TransportSelector` with priority-based scoring algorithm for auto-selection\n- Introduced `TransportContext` and `EnvironmentDetector` for runtime environment detection\n- Enables automatic transport selection based on platform, browser capabilities, and performance requirements\n\n### Grove: Common Transport Adapter\n- Added `TransportAdapter` to bridge Grove's concrete transports with Common's abstract `TransportStrategy` trait\n- Implements bidirectional translation between Grove types and Common DTOs\n- Aligns with architectural separation: Common defines traits, Grove provides implementation\n\n## Build Pipeline Transformation\n\n### Output: Source Compilation Migration\n- Migrated from prebuilt VSCode output to source compilation using Rest compiler\n- Updated ESBuild configuration to compile from VSCode source (`Dependency/Microsoft/Dependency/Editor/src`)\n- Removed dependency on VSCode's `out/` and `out-build/` directories\n- Resolved pnpm workspace conflicts caused by test `package.json` files in prebuilt output\n\n### Sky: Enforce Source-Based Compilation\n- Removed fallback path to prebuilt Microsoft Editor output in CopyVSCode.js\n- Now exclusively uses compiled VSCode artifacts from Output package\n- Added comprehensive .gitignore for build artifacts\n\n### Rest: OXC Compiler Test Suite\n- Added comprehensive unit tests for OXC compiler (parser, transformer, codegen, decorators, source maps)\n- Implemented VSCode compatibility integration tests\n- Validates OXC migration and ensures VSCode build pipeline compatibility\n\n## Project Hygiene\n\n### Wind & Worker: Git Ignore\n- Added .gitignore files to exclude build artifacts, node_modules, IDE configurations, and logs\n- Preserves debug/release folders for specific build configurations\n\n## Impact\n\nEstablishes unified transport layer across Common/Grove, completes the source-based VSCode compilation pipeline (Rest → Output → Sky → Cocoon), and maintains repository cleanliness across UI elements.",
			"SHA": "98ac1632290491ad5792f151a3bae512249f9de1"
